# OPNsense firewalls to back up, one per line. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
#   <name>  <base URL>  [tls]
#
# name  Short label: [A-Za-z0-9._-]. The backup is saved as config_<name>.xml and
#       the API key is read from $API_KEY_DIR/<name>.txt.
# URL   https://host[:port] of the web GUI / API.
# tls   How to trust the GUI certificate:
#         sha256//<base64>   pin the certificate's public key (best for the default
#                            self-signed cert; survives a renewal that keeps the key)
#         ca:/path/ca.pem    verify against a CA file (hostname must match the cert)
#         system             verify against the system CA store (default)
#         insecure           no verification (not recommended)
#
# Get a pin with:
#   echo | openssl s_client -connect HOST:443 2>/dev/null | openssl x509 -pubkey -noout \
#     | openssl pkey -pubin -outform der | openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | base64
#
# Example:
# fw1   https://192.0.2.1        sha256//AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA=
# fw2   https://fw2.example.com  system
